<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John IV, Count of Katzenelnbogen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1444">1444</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Johann IV of Katzenelnbogen</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John IV (died 1444) was Count of Katzenelnbogen, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhineland">Rhineland</a> county whose rulers drew great wealth from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> tolls. An account from his cellar at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russelsheim">Rüsselsheim</a> dated 1435, recording the purchase of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/riesling">Riesling</a> vines, is the earliest known written mention of the grape. He was succeeded by his son Philip the Elder, the last count.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/john-iv-count-of-katzenelnbogen.jpg" alt="John IV, Count of Katzenelnbogen" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Oliver Abels (SBT) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kloster_Eberbach_Basilika_Grabplatte_57.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
